{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>And behold the plague has dimmed and the plague has not spread in the skin — and he is pure.</b> And if you ask: if for not spreading he is pure, then all the more so when it dims is he pure? Rather, <b>and has not spread</b> here refers back to the first quarantine. And this is what it says: <b>and behold</b> in the second quarantine <b>the plague has dimmed</b> — that it did not spread in the first quarantine — on this the Merciful One said <b>and he is pure.</b> And one should not say that <b>and the plague has not spread</b> refers to the second quarantine, for Rashi explained here: it has dimmed from its appearance — but if it stayed at its appearance or spread, he is impure. But Chazak (firmly held), for so we say in Megillah: the verse says ״והצרוע אשר בו הנגע״ — one whose tzara'at hangs on his body, and Rashi explained: as long as he has not recovered from it he is impure, and that is absolute. And concerning his purification it is written ״והנה נרפא נגע הצרעת מן הצרוע״ — he leaves quarantine, for his purification depends on the days of quarantine: if on the seventh day no signs of impurity — white hair or spreading — are found in him, he is declared pure even though the plague in his eyes stands unchanged. Another interpretation: <b>and behold the plague has dimmed</b> — one might say, since it changed from its appearance it is a new plague and he should be impure; therefore it says <b>and behold it has dimmed</b> etc." "<b>And he is pure.</b> By speech." "<b>And he shall wash his garments.</b> All the more so his body — because he stood in doubtful impurity, and anyone who stands in doubtful impurity is not so careful regarding it."], :book :leviticus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 13, :notes {0 "הז׳ק resolved as חז״ק (חזק, 'firmly held'), following the logical flow of the argument. פרש״י and חז״ק are reverent abbreviations using the letter kuf; resolved mechanically as Rashi and Chazak respectively."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:11:46.763436093Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}